WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.962 --> 00:00:27.362
Hi, welcome back to Arja Nagarjuna.

00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:29.403
And here we go.

00:00:29.403 --> 00:00:32.130
We're now reached the 17th chapter

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.869
which is LAS KYI BRTAGS PA

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:38.869
It's a investigation
into the nature of karma

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.000
and the seeds for karma.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.000
And we went through and we
were saying that this chapter

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:52.050
is unusual because we can understand it.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.875
It doesn't even seem like Nagarjuna.

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:57.162
Don't worry. He's going to lose us later.

00:00:57.162 --> 00:00:59.320
And personally,

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.450
I was wondering why he
went through sort of

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.070
the Abhidharma presentation on karma,

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:09.980
dividing it into intention,
and the actions of body

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.630
and speech that are intended.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.053
And then he went through
some kind of obscure

00:01:17.053 --> 00:01:22.053
Abhidharma ideas about
different kinds of karma

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.040
that you can see a person's intention,

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.040
or a halo, or an aura forms
around them, good or bad.

00:01:30.073 --> 00:01:32.370
And then that's another kind of karma.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.004
Do you guys want to, anybody
want to make a 100 dollars

00:01:35.004 --> 00:01:40.004
and guess why he's going through obscure
Abhidharma presentations of karma?

00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:44.818
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:01:44.818 --> 00:01:48.401
No, that's -- Why? Why
is he working on that?

00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:52.912
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.731
The answer is more easy than that.

00:01:56.731 --> 00:01:59.250
- [Student] Because everyone
was an Abhidharma student.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.191
- Yay! How much I say? A hundred dollars?

00:02:01.191 --> 00:02:02.024
- [Student] Yes.

00:02:02.024 --> 00:02:04.524
- Pachi, $100. Don't forget to tell Elly.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.450
Yeah, everybody was
Abhidharma at that time

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.160
for seven hundred years.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.500
And then he was trying to
reverse that tidal wave.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.070
And he did, by the way, single-handedly.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.523
He stood in front of

00:02:15.523 --> 00:02:20.010
a whole ocean of accountants
from the Abhidharma school,

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.426
and he turned them all into hippies, yay.

00:02:23.426 --> 00:02:24.967
So anyway.

00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:27.229
So here he is going, okay,

00:02:27.229 --> 00:02:30.940
and we were wondering if you remember

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.510
why he didn't just
describe the ten good deeds

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.530
and ten bad deeds,

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.181
and guess what he does next, you ready?

00:02:37.181 --> 00:02:39.256
,DKAR PO'I LAS KYI LAM BCU PO,

00:02:39.256 --> 00:02:40.956
,CHOS SGRUB PA YI THABS YIN TE,

00:02:40.956 --> 00:02:43.047
,CHOS KYI 'BRAS BU 'DI GZHAN DU,

00:02:43.047 --> 00:02:46.012
,'DOD PA'I YON TAN RNAM LNGA'O,

00:02:46.012 --> 00:02:50.790
DKAR PO'I LAS means white
karma or good karma.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.543
LAM BCU PO -- the 10 paths.

00:02:53.543 --> 00:02:54.690
So the 10 good deeds,

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.597
the 10 commandments in Buddhism are called

00:02:57.597 --> 00:03:00.223
the 10 paths of white karma.

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:05.290
CHOS SGRUB ... CHOS SGRUB PA YI THABS

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:08.680
These are a method of achieving dharma.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.550
And then Choney Lama says,

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.250
"When Nagarjuna says dharma
here, Arya Nagarjuna,

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:19.250
he means a higher births
and definite good."

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:22.380
Definite good is called NGES LEGS,

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.150
and it means nirvana and Buddhahood.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:28.410
So when Nagarjuna says

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.380
in the first line and a half

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.020
there are 10 paths of white karma and

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.730
these are a method of
achieving the Dharma,

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:41.730
he means a higher birth,
and nirvana, and Buddhahood.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.090
CHOS KYI 'BRAS BU 'DI GZHAN DU

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.660
Then the line just says,

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.470
"The result of this
Dharma is this and other."

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:54.490
Anybody want to take a guess
of what this an other is?

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:58.775
You get good results in
this life and other lives.

00:03:58.775 --> 00:03:59.975
dirstha-adirstha. Right?

00:03:59.975 --> 00:04:03.438
Seen in this life and
seen in future lives.

00:04:03.438 --> 00:04:05.330
'DOD PA'I YON TAN RNAM LNGA'O

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:09.347
And especially, you're going
to get 'DOD PA'I YON TAN,

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.210
the good stuff of the desire realm.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.980
Nice things to eat,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.940
nice music to listen to,
soft blankets, you know,

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.250
just think of the wonders
of your future life

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.882
when you follow these
10 good deeds, you know,

00:04:26.882 --> 00:04:29.846
what a cushy life you're going to have.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:36.000
You're going to get expensive
creams for your face.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.573
And I don't know about you,
but I start to... I'm like,

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.426
that's weird.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.920
It doesn't seem, it doesn't seem like

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.450
Nagarjuna to say

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.300
you're going to get a new car,

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.105
your hair is going to grow back,

00:04:51.105 --> 00:04:54.656
you're going to get energy, you know?

00:04:54.656 --> 00:04:59.656
And then we find out from Choney Lama,

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:05.010
he is criticizing. Okay, got it?

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.140
He's saying "Oh, great,

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.490
the 10 good deeds." - What? -
More money, more car, more hair.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.067
You're going to be healthy.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:16.970
And then we find out from Choney Lama,

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:21.593
this is Nagarjuna sort of saying,

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.910
"Look how people talk about karma.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.780
Look how these guys talk about karma."

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:30.610
You look at the purposes
they want to put karma to,

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.730
and then he's criticizing them.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.910
And what he criticizes
is deeper than you think.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.680
It's fine to get a lot of money.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.360
It's fine to get a nice car.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.130
It's fine to have a good apartment.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:46.070
But it's not fine to think
that there's a self existent

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:50.230
relationship between doing the
"10" and getting that stuff.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.843
- Is it okay to have a
nice apartment? - Yes.

00:05:52.843 --> 00:05:54.970
- Can I be, can I have a big bank account?

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:57.410
- Yeah, that's fine. You
can help more people.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.320
- Can I have a big car?

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.080
- Yeah. You can fit more people or
go to parties at John Brady's house.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.383
And then [laughs], okay,

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.730
but if you think there's
a self existing connection

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.600
between helping other people

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.930
or doing the Medicine Buddha mantra,

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.560
and getting all these nice things,

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:20.720
if you think that connection
doesn't come from you,

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.820
then something's going to
happen in the next verse.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.660
So the next verse kind of reveals

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.250
what we're really thinking about.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.164
By the way, I like this...

00:06:29.164 --> 00:06:34.164
Choney Lama says he has a side
comment on that last verse.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.760
And there's the picture
that he's using with the guy

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:39.400
with the airplane tickets.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.390
And he says, "By the way,

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:45.730
this verse in general is a
criticism of people who are

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:49.580
focusing on karma to get stuff.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.020
Not because the stuff is wrong,

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.450
but because their feeling
about the connection

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.403
between the karma and
the stuff is too solid."

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.420
They don't understand the
emptiness of that connection.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.130
He says so that's okay.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:07.690
We could also say... we could've
added another line to this

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.830
verse that said you will get
house, you'll get apartment,

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.478
you know, you'll get healthy,

00:07:12.478 --> 00:07:15.227
and you'll get enlightened [laughs].

00:07:15.227 --> 00:07:16.060
He said if it was me,

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.140
I would have added a line to the verse.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.620
One more line.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.790
So just be aware of that
guy with the airplane ticket

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:27.063
and a passport: that's a
passport to enlightenment.

00:07:27.063 --> 00:07:30.380
Which is also comes from the
10 good deeds. All right.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:34.400
Then the next verse
reveals Nagarjuna's opinion

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.880
about the last verse.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.782
And here it goes.

00:07:37.782 --> 00:07:39.331
,GAL TE BRTAG PA DER 'GYUR NA,

00:07:39.331 --> 00:07:43.191
,NYES PA CHEN PO MANG POR 'GYUR,

00:07:43.191 --> 00:07:46.640
If you do that kind of BRTAG PA,

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.380
what's BRTAG PA?

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.613
B-R-T-A-G

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:53.494
ba rata ta BRTA ga BRTAG

00:07:53.494 --> 00:07:54.700
- [Woman] Pariksha.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:55.760
- Yeah, pariksha.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:00.730
If you do, if that's
the best investigation

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:03.627
you can do on karma,

00:08:03.627 --> 00:08:05.210
NYES PA CHEN PO MANG PO

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:09.080
you're going to get into
a big pile of problems,

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.520
many big piles of problems [laughs].

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.560
So Nagarjuna is like,

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.430
the other guy can just see him, he's like,

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.450
well, I was just saying you
should do the 10 good deeds

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.080
because you can get
lots of money and stuff.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.760
He says, God, think
like, you do the pariksha

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:25.100
like that, big trouble, big, big,

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.330
so many problems is
going to come from that.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.900
Doing your Medicine Buddha mantra is

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.320
because you think you're going to be

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.633
healthy later, just for that,

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.300
and to think there's
a connection like that

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.690
between the mantra and the good health,

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:41.680
NYES PA CHEN PO MANG POR 'GYUR,

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.550
you're going to get into
a lot of problems later.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:45.615
Like what?

00:08:45.615 --> 00:08:47.339
,DE LTA BAS NA BRTAG PA DE,

00:08:47.339 --> 00:08:49.170
,'DIR NI 'THAD PA MA YIN NO,

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.610
Then Nagarjuna goes further.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.720
He says, your kind of pariksha

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.793
is an anti-pariksha.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:56.573
Okay?

00:08:56.573 --> 00:09:00.666
Your investigation is
"estupido" investigation.

00:09:00.666 --> 00:09:01.499
[students laughing]

00:09:01.499 --> 00:09:02.332
Okay, got it?

00:09:02.332 --> 00:09:04.330
- That's an idiot's investigation.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:05.163
- What?

00:09:05.163 --> 00:09:07.330
- You're going to use karma
just to get some money

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:12.243
or just to cure your hair or something.

00:09:12.243 --> 00:09:16.090
It's just, by the way,
not wrong to get money,

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:19.100
not wrong to get hair,

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:23.373
just wrong to think there's
an automatic connection.

00:09:23.373 --> 00:09:25.880
It's how you think about the mantra.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.547
It's not the mantra.

00:09:27.547 --> 00:09:29.000
All right.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.653
And I have two kids here.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.636
These are twins.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:41.280
And you know, when you see them,

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.800
you assume it's a picture of two twins,

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.210
but that's an assumption.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.870
They may not be twins at all.

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:50.870
They may just be from,
they may just look similar.

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:54.490
Yeah, you can do the mantra
and something might happen.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:56.980
But is there a connection between the two?

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:00.292
Is it really what you think you see?

00:10:00.292 --> 00:10:01.300
All right.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.628
And that takes us to the next verse.

00:10:08.521 --> 00:10:10.245
,SANGS RGYAS RNAMS DANG RANG RGYAL DANG,

00:10:10.245 --> 00:10:11.545
,NYAN THOS RNAMS KYIS GANG GSUNGS PA'I,

00:10:11.545 --> 00:10:13.679
,BRTAG PA GANG ZHIG 'DIR 'THAD PA,

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:16.050
,DE NI RAB TU BRJOD PAR BYA,

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.163
By the way,

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:22.580
there is an investigation into karma

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.020
that you could've done

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.120
which would've been a
better investigation,

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.248
not "estupedo".

00:10:28.248 --> 00:10:30.670
You could've had a smart investigation.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.490
- Which one is that?

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:35.520
- Well, it was described by the Buddha

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.540
and by the self-made buddhas

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:40.110
and by the great listeners,
these are arhats,

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:41.810
people who reached nirvana.

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:45.930
If you're going to do an
investigation into karma,

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.570
I suggest you follow their investigation

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.847
and not your investigation [laughs].

00:10:50.847 --> 00:10:51.680
Okay?

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:54.190
Not think there's a
self existing connection

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:57.480
between Medicine Buddha
mantra and those, you know,

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.303
money and good health.

00:11:00.303 --> 00:11:02.800
- I suggest you shift your investigation.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:03.890
- To what?

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.220
- To the one that the Buddha described.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.099
All right.

00:11:08.099 --> 00:11:09.530
- Well, what's that?

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:11.820
DE NI RAB TU BRJOD PAR BYA

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.130
I'm going to tell you.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:17.157
I'm going to tell you so perfectly.

00:11:17.157 --> 00:11:22.138
RAB TU means I'm going to
set you straight, 100%.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:27.860
Then he goes off on a very deep
subject and difficult subject.

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:29.461
So finally,

00:11:29.461 --> 00:11:32.287
Nagarjuna took off the gloves,

00:11:32.287 --> 00:11:34.330
and he's going to show you his real style.

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.720
So here he goes.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.350
Fasten your seatbelts.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:39.766
Here we go. Okay.

00:11:39.766 --> 00:11:42.558
,DPANG RGYA JI LTAR DE BZHIN CHUD,

00:11:43.732 --> 00:11:44.940
,MI ZA

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:47.132
,MI ZA LAS NI BU LON BZHIN,

00:11:47.132 --> 00:11:50.750
And there's a bunch of
problems in the carvings,

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.300
but I figured it out.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:55.940
So DPANG RGYA means a contract.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.830
And it's often used for loans.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:03.130
When you borrow money 2000 years ago,

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.030
you have to sign a DPANG RGYA.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:08.930
Or when you get married, you
have to sign a DPANG RGYA.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.250
So it could be a marriage contract

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:14.530
and it could be a loan agreement.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:19.530
He says DPANG RGYA DE BZHIN

00:12:20.046 --> 00:12:23.088
DPANG RGYA JI LTAR DE BZHIN CHUD

00:12:23.088 --> 00:12:24.600
And you have to read across the lines.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.488
You have to say CHUD MI ZA.

00:12:27.488 --> 00:12:29.090
And you guys know CHUD MI ZA,

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:32.020
I taught to you in the LAM RIM
over, and over, and over again.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.545
Four laws of karma.

00:12:34.545 --> 00:12:37.820
BYAS PA CHUD MI ZA BA

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.420
The fourth of the laws of karma.

00:12:40.408 --> 00:12:45.408
If you do do something,
you will get a result.

00:12:46.029 --> 00:12:47.210
BYAS PA CHUD MI ZA BA

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:50.541
Literally, BYAS PA means
if you do something,

00:12:50.541 --> 00:12:51.860
CHUD MI ZA BA means

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:55.010
it's not just kind of fade away over time.

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:59.720
You can't hope that you
can lie to your mom,

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:03.078
and then the karma is just going
to wear out sooner or later

00:13:03.078 --> 00:13:06.600
before 20 people lie back to you.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.040
Like you can't,

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:12.310
you shouldn't hope that
you can do something wrong,

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.320
keep it quiet, don't tell anybody,

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:16.870
and after time everyone's going to forget,

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:20.293
because that's not how karma works.

00:13:20.293 --> 00:13:23.922
Everything's recorded
and everything expands.

00:13:23.922 --> 00:13:28.922
So, you know, he says that principle,

00:13:29.207 --> 00:13:30.877
CHUD MI ZA BA, don't forget that word

00:13:30.877 --> 00:13:32.480
because we're going to
have to come back to it

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:33.570
over and over again,

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:36.600
in this part. CHUD MI ZA BA means

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:40.610
in Tibetan, karma's not
just going to fade away

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.860
if you wait long enough.

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:44.670
In fact, the opposite.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.700
So don't think CHUD MI ZA BA.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:51.700
Now, he says that, in Abhidharma,

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.320
you can take a general proof
and in the Abhidharma school

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.300
it becomes a tool.

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:01.970
The fact that CHUD MI ZA BA,

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.680
the fact that karma doesn't just fade away

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:08.320
in Abhidharma system is a separate thing.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:11.940
It's a real thing, like a cup or a table.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.700
Hey, did you bring your cup?

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.630
- Yeah. Did you put it on the table?

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:19.283
- Yeah. - How's your CHUD MI ZA BA doing?

00:14:19.283 --> 00:14:20.220
- What?

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:23.460
- How's the fact that your
karma is not going to fade away?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:26.598
How's that feel this morning?

00:14:26.598 --> 00:14:28.890
And in fact, in the Abhidharma system,

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:32.590
every time you do anything,
you also do a CHUD MI ZA BA.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.720
You give money, you do a CHUD MI ZA BA.

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:37.553
Got it?

00:14:37.553 --> 00:14:39.520
You do a nice thing for somebody,

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.150
you pick up another CHUD MI ZA BA.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.790
You put it... here's
another CHUD MI ZA BA,

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:46.200
means that good deed is
not going to just go away.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.740
So good could be for
good deeds or bad deeds.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.210
And they do that in Abhidharma.

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:52.570
They have the idea like THOB PA.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.833
When you achieve nirvana, what
connects you to the nirvana?

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:00.560
Then in fact, there's
a problem in Abhidharma

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.030
because you're not there anymore.

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:06.810
Then you got to get an achievement.

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:08.980
And it's an entity.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.230
It's like a cup.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:13.072
- Do you have an achievement?

00:15:13.072 --> 00:15:14.728
Did you reach nirvana yesterday? - Yes.

00:15:14.728 --> 00:15:18.050
- Did they give you an achievement? - No.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:20.830
- Oh my God, that you're going
to, it's going to fall off.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.080
Get an achievement [laughs].

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.090
So it's called a THOB PA.

00:15:26.248 --> 00:15:29.260
So now we're going to go
off on a subject called...

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.854
What do you want to call that in English?

00:15:30.854 --> 00:15:33.950
CHUD MI ZA BA, it don't go away?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:37.350
Did you get "a don't go away"?

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.240
Did you pick up "a don't go away"

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.393
when you donated the money to ALL?

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.298
Were you careful to get "a don't go away"

00:15:45.298 --> 00:15:48.241
from Pau when you made
the donation to the club?

00:15:49.154 --> 00:15:50.030
Club de oro?

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:52.710
Did she also give you "a don't go away"?

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:55.640
Did you get a don't, did you
pick up "a don't go away"?

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:56.720
Okay. Got it?

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.330
It's a contract, in a way.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.550
- We guarantee that you're
going to have prosperity.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:02.383
- Why?

00:16:02.383 --> 00:16:04.700
- You just donated money to
the most important project

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.580
in the universe.

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:08.230
So we give you a written guarantee,

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:11.329
that's called a DPANG RGYA or
CHUD MI ZA BA'I DPANG RGYA.

00:16:11.329 --> 00:16:14.510
That's a don't go away contract.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.553
Okay. Got it?

00:16:16.553 --> 00:16:18.670
Because we're going to spend
now like a couple of hours

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:20.593
on don't go away contracts.

00:16:21.442 --> 00:16:23.108
Phew.

00:16:23.108 --> 00:16:26.600
BU LON BZHIN means it's
like when you take a loan.

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:30.000
BU LON BZHIN means it's similar
to when you take a loan.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.170
They give you a contract and you sign it.

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:37.036
When you take the money,
you get the contract,

00:16:37.036 --> 00:16:39.000
the don't go away contract.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:43.283
That don't go away means you
don't go away without paying back.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:45.293
All right.

00:16:45.293 --> 00:16:46.392
So you can have a don't go away

00:16:46.392 --> 00:16:49.561
with good things and with bad things.

00:16:49.561 --> 00:16:50.500
All right, here we go.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.699
We're going to dig deeper into?

00:16:52.699 --> 00:16:54.230
- [Students] Don't go aways.

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:56.370
- Don't go aways.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.061
It's a noun, right? All right.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:02.440
And that's going to be pretty
much the rest of the chapter.

00:17:05.724 --> 00:17:10.716
Now, Nagarjuna is going to
repeat what the last 700 years

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:16.350
of guys said about don't go aways.

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:17.183
Don't go aways

00:17:17.183 --> 00:17:19.260
- What's the don't go away look like?

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.820
- Well, I'll tell you.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:24.780
,DE NI KHAMS LAS RNAM PA BZHI,

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:28.973
According to KHAMS meaning
dhatu, meaning realm.

00:17:28.973 --> 00:17:31.180
Those can be divided into three.

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:34.750
You've got don't go aways
in the desire realm,

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:37.870
you've got don't go
aways in the form realm,

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:40.490
you've got don't go aways
in the formless realm,

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:44.030
but he says four. Why?
In the Abhidharma system,

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:47.100
you can have something outside the realms.

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.780
And that's pure things,
ZAG BCAS, "vimala" things,

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:54.770
like nirvana or Buddhahood.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:57.710
He says you can get a don't go away

00:17:57.710 --> 00:18:00.870
that's not in sansara.
It's outside the sansara.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:02.790
So let's call it four,

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.280
three for the sansaric realms

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.640
and one that's outside of sansara.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.810
Four don't go aways.

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:12.248
Whose idea?

00:18:12.248 --> 00:18:14.621
Abhidharma. Abhidharma.

00:18:14.621 --> 00:18:19.621
Choney Lama said BYE
BRAG SMRA BA 'GA' ZHIG

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:23.987
meaning some Detailists,
some Abhidharma guys.

00:18:23.987 --> 00:18:26.581
All right, so first you can
divide it into four types

00:18:26.581 --> 00:18:31.270
depending on where that
don't go away is residing.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:32.736
What's next?

00:18:32.736 --> 00:18:34.180
,DE YANG RANG BZHIN LUNG MA BSTAN,

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:36.439
What's LUNG MA BSTAN? You guys know this.

00:18:36.439 --> 00:18:39.361
DGE BA, it's not DGE BA.
It's not MI DGE BA.

00:18:39.361 --> 00:18:42.272
- [Student] Neutral.
- Yeah, karmically neutral.

00:18:42.272 --> 00:18:44.860
And that's a little tricky.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:49.860
A lot of these instruments

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:53.600
which keeps spiritual stuff on you

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:56.820
are karmically neutral themselves.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.930
So a don't go away,

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:00.930
a contract isn't good or bad.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.210
I mean there can be bad
stuff in the contract,

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:04.870
or there can be good
stuff in the contract,

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:08.120
but the papers like, you
know, the instrument,

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.230
the vehicle for the contract,

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:14.550
which is a don't go away, is neutral.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:15.780
He's like paper.

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:17.560
Then you can write
something nasty on the paper

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:19.240
or you can write something
nice on the paper,

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:22.230
but the don't go away is neutral.

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:25.315
And then it could be a bad
one. It could be a good one.

00:19:25.315 --> 00:19:27.263
All right. Next verse.

00:19:29.935 --> 00:19:31.451
,SPONG BAS SPANG BA MA YIN TE,

00:19:31.451 --> 00:19:34.810
,BSGOM PAS SPANG BA NYID KYANG YIN,

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:37.160
There's a mistake in the carving.

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:39.251
Let me fix that one.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:41.843
Okay.

00:19:45.281 --> 00:19:47.960
SPONG BAS SPANG BA MA
YIN TE, very important.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:52.111
It is not eliminated by MTHONG LAM.

00:19:52.111 --> 00:19:53.380
Yeah.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:55.350
You can see emptiness directly,

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:00.063
and it doesn't do anything
to your don't go aways.

00:20:00.911 --> 00:20:02.123
Okay.

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.620
Delicate question.

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:08.713
But by the way, Nagarjuna
is trying to impress on us.

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:13.680
What's a don't go away? What
makes karma stick to you?

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.609
What makes karma stick to you?

00:20:15.609 --> 00:20:17.500
Well, it's don't go aways.

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:19.130
What's a don't go away like?

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:20.470
Well, it's karmacally neutral.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.602
It could be in different realms

00:20:22.602 --> 00:20:26.270
and unfortunately you don't
drop the don't go aways

00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:29.463
when you see emptiness directly.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:33.140
But maybe you get rid of the bad karma,

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:35.678
but keep the don't go away?

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:38.680
Okay. Question.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.320
We're not sure yet.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:41.153
Okay.

00:20:41.153 --> 00:20:43.888
And BSGOM PAS SPANG BA NYID KYANG YIN,

00:20:45.695 --> 00:20:48.240
it is eliminated by the
path of habituation.

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:51.460
$100, tell me why it should be.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:52.293
$100.

00:20:52.293 --> 00:20:55.600
Don't forget what school we're in.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.830
Don't forget what school we're in.

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:01.650
And what if I say a don't go away

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:04.320
can be eliminated at the end of

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.350
the path of habituation.

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:08.710
- Why? What happens there?

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:12.196
Lower school, lower school.

00:21:12.196 --> 00:21:13.340
- [Woman] End of suffering.

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:15.115
- I want more precision.

00:21:15.115 --> 00:21:17.473
For a $100 I need at least two words.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:21.880
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:25.463
Lower school, lower school.

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:29.467
Okay. I'm cutting it to $50.

00:21:29.467 --> 00:21:31.418
BEM RIG RGYUN CHAD PA

00:21:31.418 --> 00:21:35.868
Cut the flow of BEM PO
and RIG PA. Lower nirvana.

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:42.565
Cut the flow of BEM PO
and RIG PA. Lower nirvana.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:45.570
For $12 [laughs].

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:49.907
Ah, forget the bet, BEM PO
means your material body.

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.543
And RIG PA means your mind.

00:21:52.543 --> 00:21:57.270
RGYUN CHAD PA means, in the
lower school, you blink out.

00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:58.103
[fingers snapping]

00:21:58.103 --> 00:21:59.340
You just blink out.

00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:02.260
Then you don't suffer anymore. Yay!

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:04.300
Then the debate by the higher schools

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:06.217
is not too complicated.

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:08.629
- What's nirvana according to you?

00:22:08.629 --> 00:22:09.462
[hands slapping]

00:22:09.462 --> 00:22:11.696
- You blink out. - What?

00:22:11.696 --> 00:22:12.529
[hands slapping]

00:22:12.529 --> 00:22:14.399
- Your body blinks out, your
mind blinks out? - Right.

00:22:14.399 --> 00:22:16.171
- What do we call you then?

00:22:16.171 --> 00:22:18.656
- Arhat. - Where's Arhat?

00:22:18.656 --> 00:22:19.489
[laughing]

00:22:19.489 --> 00:22:20.518
- [Woman] Nowhere.

00:22:20.518 --> 00:22:23.551
- [laughs] It's a very funny,
that's an ancient debate.

00:22:23.551 --> 00:22:24.726
[hands clapping]

00:22:24.726 --> 00:22:26.809
- Where's the Arhat [laughs]?

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:28.838
All right.

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:33.472
So probably your don't go aways
are going to finish if your...

00:22:33.472 --> 00:22:34.755
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:22:34.755 --> 00:22:37.060
body and mind finish [laughs].

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:38.972
All right

00:22:38.972 --> 00:22:40.497
,DE PHYIR CHUD MI ZA BA YIS,

00:22:40.497 --> 00:22:42.638
,LAS KYI 'BRAS BU SKYED PAR 'GYUR,

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:48.850
Don't forget, we were having
this trouble of saying

00:22:48.850 --> 00:22:53.580
if the karmic seed changes, right?

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:56.870
Sorry, if it doesn't change,
it can't give a result.

00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:59.375
And if it does change, moment by moment,

00:22:59.375 --> 00:23:00.330
[fingers snapping]

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:04.730
it disappears in one 65th of a second.

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:07.570
So how can it transmit your...

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:10.410
how can there be a CHUD MI ZA BA?

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:12.713
How can there be a, what do we call it?

00:23:12.713 --> 00:23:15.240
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:16.750
No, what's the word we use?

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:20.240
How can the don't go away flow over time

00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:25.240
if it's instant, coming in and out
of existence, moment by moment?

00:23:25.306 --> 00:23:28.247
Then he says here

00:23:28.247 --> 00:23:30.070
DE PHYIR CHUD MI ZA BA YIS

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:34.020
it's not the karmic seed that
creates the karmic result.

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:36.561
It's the don't go away.

00:23:36.561 --> 00:23:38.330
[students laughing]

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:42.980
It's the seed comes and go,
but the don't go away stay.

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:44.940
Then when the seed disappears,

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:47.354
the don't go away stays with you.

00:23:47.354 --> 00:23:49.910
And then the don't go away
gives you the money later.

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:53.500
After you give a donation, got it?

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:56.130
The don't go away can stay.

00:23:56.130 --> 00:23:57.770
Got it? [laughs]

00:23:57.770 --> 00:23:59.210
Okay. This is okay.

00:23:59.210 --> 00:24:03.441
I can see you're impressed
with this idea [laughs].

00:24:03.441 --> 00:24:04.758
,GAL TE SPONG BAS SPANG BA DANG,

00:24:04.758 --> 00:24:08.240
,LAS 'PHO BA YIS 'JIG 'GYUR NA,

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:11.183
If the don't go aways could disappear,

00:24:12.570 --> 00:24:16.260
just because you reached a
higher path in the five paths,

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:19.827
or just because something's
happened to your karma in general,

00:24:19.827 --> 00:24:24.343
then DE LA LAS 'JIG LA SOGS PA'I

00:24:26.017 --> 00:24:29.300
Then LAS BYAS PA CHUD ZA BA.

00:24:30.425 --> 00:24:32.450
Say LAS BYAS PA CHUD ZA
BA. [students repeat]

00:24:32.450 --> 00:24:36.123
Then you could hurt somebody
and never get a result

00:24:37.940 --> 00:24:42.060
which breaks every law of karma and
everything the Buddha ever said.

00:24:42.060 --> 00:24:45.459
If the don't go away could be eliminated

00:24:45.459 --> 00:24:48.410
even by great spiritual attainments,

00:24:48.410 --> 00:24:53.410
then you're saying you could do
a bad deed and get no result.

00:24:53.900 --> 00:24:55.400
Not possible. Okay?

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:59.920
So the don't go away has to stay [laughs].

00:24:59.920 --> 00:25:02.782
Maybe it doesn't create
anything, I don't know.

00:25:02.782 --> 00:25:04.088
,SKYON RNAMS SU NI THAL BAR 'GYUR,

00:25:04.088 --> 00:25:05.660
look at all the problems you're causing.

00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:08.700
Then he says SOGS, he
says other problems too.

00:25:08.700 --> 00:25:10.060
And then Choney Lama says,

00:25:10.060 --> 00:25:12.650
"Are you curious about what
the other problem was?"

00:25:12.650 --> 00:25:15.407
And we're like, "Yeah, we
were really wondering."

00:25:15.407 --> 00:25:20.217
And he says LAS MA BYAS
BA DANG MA PHRAD PA

00:25:20.217 --> 00:25:23.930
Problem number three, law
number three of karma.

00:25:23.930 --> 00:25:26.460
Yeah, if you don't do it, you're
not going to get a problem.

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:28.720
If you don't steal money,

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:30.723
you're never going to lose money.

00:25:31.750 --> 00:25:35.000
Karmic law number three:
if you don't do it,

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:36.420
you don't get a result.

00:25:36.420 --> 00:25:37.830
Karmic law number four,

00:25:37.830 --> 00:25:41.300
if you do do it, it's not
going to just fade away.

00:25:41.300 --> 00:25:42.230
Okay. Got it?

00:25:42.230 --> 00:25:46.969
So the CHUD MI ZA BA
principle of... what was it?

00:25:46.969 --> 00:25:48.116
Don't go away.

00:25:48.116 --> 00:25:52.570
The don't go away is so useful
because we can still keep

00:25:52.570 --> 00:25:54.846
the last two laws of karma.

00:25:59.129 --> 00:26:00.883
Okay.

00:26:00.883 --> 00:26:02.218
All right, here we go.

00:26:02.218 --> 00:26:04.309
By the way, I have a Titanic sinking here.

00:26:04.309 --> 00:26:06.660
Are you ready, Pachi?

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:08.010
I worked so hard.

00:26:08.010 --> 00:26:08.843
You know,

00:26:08.843 --> 00:26:10.957
there's no pictures of
the Titanic sinking?

00:26:10.957 --> 00:26:12.990
[students laughing]

00:26:12.990 --> 00:26:16.439
So I got this one for you guys [laughs].

00:26:18.792 --> 00:26:22.225
And okay, by the way,

00:26:23.750 --> 00:26:28.190
if the Titanic, if you had a credit card,

00:26:28.190 --> 00:26:31.720
when you got on the Titanic
and you used it a lot

00:26:31.720 --> 00:26:36.053
on the Titanic, and then it sank,

00:26:37.110 --> 00:26:38.790
how's your DPANG RGYA?

00:26:38.790 --> 00:26:41.690
How's your credit card bill?
What's it going to look like?

00:26:43.033 --> 00:26:43.866
- [Student] Zero.

00:26:43.866 --> 00:26:45.280
- Zero! Okay, got it?

00:26:45.280 --> 00:26:49.130
Your don't go aways sank with the Titanic.

00:26:49.130 --> 00:26:51.230
That represents nirvana:

00:26:51.230 --> 00:26:54.560
the discontinuation of your body and mind.

00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:57.330
That's the sinking of the Titanic.

00:26:57.330 --> 00:27:00.610
It also takes your credit card bills.

00:27:00.610 --> 00:27:04.320
Nobody on the Titanic got
charged for the food and drink,

00:27:04.320 --> 00:27:07.240
I wonder, probably not, right?

00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:10.601
The company probably failed the next day.

00:27:10.601 --> 00:27:14.220
So anyway, I thought it was a cute example

00:27:14.220 --> 00:27:17.520
of discontinuation of body and mind.

00:27:17.520 --> 00:27:19.040
And then all those DPANG RGYAs,

00:27:19.040 --> 00:27:21.240
all those credit card agreements

00:27:21.240 --> 00:27:22.950
went down with the ship.

00:27:22.950 --> 00:27:27.380
Then maybe nirvana is defined by finally

00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:30.669
you escaped your credit
card bills [laughs].

00:27:30.669 --> 00:27:35.669
Why? There's no body or mind
left to pay them. Got it?

00:27:35.720 --> 00:27:36.553
Okay.

00:27:36.553 --> 00:27:37.853
Isn't it cute photo? Yes.

00:27:38.730 --> 00:27:41.480
I thought we should take
a vacation to the Sanskrit

00:27:42.530 --> 00:27:44.200
for don't go away.

00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:48.420
What's the Sanskrit for a don't go away?

00:27:48.420 --> 00:27:50.380
And here you go.

00:27:50.380 --> 00:27:53.950
Avipraṇāśa (avipranasha), avipranasha.

00:27:53.950 --> 00:27:56.680
It's probably an Israeli, right, avi?

00:27:56.680 --> 00:28:00.150
Hey, Avi, pranasha.

00:28:00.150 --> 00:28:04.330
So it's four parts a-vi-pra-nasha.

00:28:04.330 --> 00:28:09.330
So please repeat, a-vi-pra-nasha.

00:28:09.817 --> 00:28:11.913
Sorry, naasha.

00:28:11.913 --> 00:28:16.557
A-vi-pra-naasha.

00:28:16.557 --> 00:28:18.888
Okay, so a- means? Christina?

00:28:18.888 --> 00:28:19.745
- [Christina] Not.

00:28:19.745 --> 00:28:22.953
- Not. Vi- means very much.

00:28:22.953 --> 00:28:27.953
Pra- means super, and the root √naś

00:28:28.230 --> 00:28:31.330
means to be lost or to fade away.

00:28:31.330 --> 00:28:32.767
Got it?

00:28:32.767 --> 00:28:36.943
Very much completely didn't fade away.

00:28:38.291 --> 00:28:41.320
Very much completely didn't fade away.

00:28:41.320 --> 00:28:45.283
A-vi-pra-naasha. Got it?

00:28:46.370 --> 00:28:48.670
So you can use the Sanskrit.

00:28:48.670 --> 00:28:51.410
Hey, you got any don't go aways?

00:28:51.410 --> 00:28:54.700
Sorry. You got any avipranashas?

00:28:54.700 --> 00:28:56.780
Yeah, I got some avipranashas.

00:28:56.780 --> 00:29:00.750
I hope I can keep the avipranashas
of my donation to the Gold Club.

00:29:00.750 --> 00:29:03.470
And I hope I can lose the avipranaashas

00:29:03.470 --> 00:29:06.961
when I reach nirvana of
all my credit cards debts.

00:29:07.800 --> 00:29:08.633
All right.

00:29:08.633 --> 00:29:10.220
So learn the word.

00:29:10.220 --> 00:29:12.820
Generally, √naś as a root in Sanskrit

00:29:12.820 --> 00:29:15.200
means to be destroyed or to be lost.

00:29:15.200 --> 00:29:19.620
It's probably connected
to "not". All right.

00:29:19.620 --> 00:29:20.773
Next verse.

00:29:21.970 --> 00:29:24.680
By the way it's a long chapter. I'm sorry.

00:29:24.680 --> 00:29:28.470
But I know you guys are fascinated.

00:29:28.470 --> 00:29:30.920
Okay. Now the other guy says,

00:29:30.920 --> 00:29:35.920
"Well, if you can lose your avipranashas,"

00:29:36.298 --> 00:29:38.677
it sounds like a Jewish pastry.

00:29:38.677 --> 00:29:39.510
[students laughing]

00:29:39.510 --> 00:29:41.760
Right? I don't know.

00:29:41.760 --> 00:29:44.600
Where's that nice bakery,
is it still there?

00:29:44.600 --> 00:29:45.524
On...?

00:29:46.780 --> 00:29:47.680
- [Woman] Oh, on second ave?

00:29:47.680 --> 00:29:49.589
- Yeah. No?

00:29:49.589 --> 00:29:51.970
- [Woman] You know, that one
was in and out of business

00:29:51.970 --> 00:29:53.395
all the time.

00:29:53.395 --> 00:29:55.223
- No, but it was there
for like a hundred years.

00:29:55.223 --> 00:29:57.026
- [Woman] Yeah, hopefully
it opens back up.

00:29:57.026 --> 00:30:00.620
- Okay. Anyway, you can pick
up some avipranashas there.

00:30:00.620 --> 00:30:04.270
Anyway, the guy says, "Okay,

00:30:04.270 --> 00:30:06.140
"I understand that if the Titanic sinks,

00:30:06.140 --> 00:30:10.203
"all the credit card bills go,
but what about life to life?

00:30:11.080 --> 00:30:14.550
"Do you lose your avipranaashas
when you skip to a new life,

00:30:14.550 --> 00:30:17.697
"when you cross the border,
NYING MTSAMS SBYOR BA,

00:30:17.697 --> 00:30:21.460
"into a new rebirth, do the
avipranashas come with you?"

00:30:21.460 --> 00:30:24.460
Do the can't go aways
come with you or not?

00:30:24.460 --> 00:30:25.936
What do you guess, by the way?

00:30:25.936 --> 00:30:27.070
- [Student] Yes.

00:30:27.070 --> 00:30:28.160
- They do go away?

00:30:28.160 --> 00:30:28.993
- [Students] No.

00:30:28.993 --> 00:30:30.240
- They probably don't go away.

00:30:30.240 --> 00:30:33.050
Otherwise, there would be
no karma in the next life.

00:30:33.050 --> 00:30:35.423
Okay. Here's the real answer.

00:30:35.423 --> 00:30:37.850
,KHAMS MTSUNGS LAS NI CHA MTSUNGS DANG,

00:30:37.850 --> 00:30:41.000
If you go from the same
rebirth to the same rebirth,

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:42.780
if you go from human to human,

00:30:42.780 --> 00:30:45.797
you keep your avipranashas.

00:30:47.660 --> 00:30:49.980
Or if you go from desire
realm to desire realm,

00:30:49.980 --> 00:30:51.786
you keep your avipranashas.

00:30:51.786 --> 00:30:53.200
,CHA MI MTSUNGS PA THAMS CAD KYI,

00:30:53.200 --> 00:30:55.160
There might be some not keeping

00:30:55.160 --> 00:30:57.980
your avipranashas when you
change to a different realm

00:30:57.980 --> 00:30:59.300
because those devas

00:30:59.300 --> 00:31:00.660
are not going to have the obvious

00:31:00.660 --> 00:31:02.780
suffering that you should
have had if you were born

00:31:02.780 --> 00:31:05.560
in the human realm, right?

00:31:05.560 --> 00:31:07.580
If you had gone from the human
realm to the human realm,

00:31:07.580 --> 00:31:12.140
you'd be having some gross
sufferings that devas don't have.

00:31:12.140 --> 00:31:14.700
So if you go from human to deva,

00:31:14.700 --> 00:31:19.676
something must have happened to some
of your avipranashas for trouble

00:31:19.676 --> 00:31:22.393
because they don't have trouble. Got it?

00:31:24.744 --> 00:31:25.577
All right.

00:31:26.607 --> 00:31:28.285
Now I mean, when you go from a human birth

00:31:28.285 --> 00:31:32.427
to a deva birth, in that birth

00:31:32.427 --> 00:31:36.200
you don't have the gross pain
that you have in this realm.

00:31:36.200 --> 00:31:38.940
Nobody breaks their arm in the deva realm.

00:31:38.940 --> 00:31:40.810
It doesn't happen.

00:31:40.810 --> 00:31:43.930
So maybe something happens
to your avipranashas,

00:31:43.930 --> 00:31:47.858
if you go to a different realm
from a human realm. All right.

00:31:47.858 --> 00:31:49.166
,CHA MI MTSUNGS PA THAMS CAD KYI,

00:31:49.166 --> 00:31:50.858
,DE NI NYING MTSAMS SBYOR BA'I TSE,

00:31:50.858 --> 00:31:52.615
,GCIG PO KHO NA SKYE BAR 'GYUR,

00:31:52.615 --> 00:31:55.010
But, okay, ready?

00:31:55.010 --> 00:31:56.330
I'm sorry.

00:31:56.330 --> 00:31:58.280
Your karma might not go with you,

00:31:58.280 --> 00:32:01.221
but your avipranasha will go with you.

00:32:01.221 --> 00:32:03.396
How's that?

00:32:06.675 --> 00:32:08.058
Your karma may not go with you,

00:32:08.058 --> 00:32:09.680
but your, what did we call it...

00:32:09.680 --> 00:32:14.020
your don't go away will
go with you. How's that?

00:32:14.020 --> 00:32:18.380
This is all Abhidharma. Okay. I'm sorry.

00:32:18.380 --> 00:32:20.527
By the way, the only reason why

00:32:20.527 --> 00:32:24.030
Nagarjuna would give a lot
of wild Abhidharma ideas

00:32:24.030 --> 00:32:26.287
as if he's going to
destroy them at some point.

00:32:26.287 --> 00:32:27.120
[everyone laughing]

00:32:27.120 --> 00:32:29.630
I'm just, I'm just telling you.

00:32:29.630 --> 00:32:30.670
All right, next verse.

00:32:30.670 --> 00:32:32.271
Sorry, next verse.

00:32:32.271 --> 00:32:36.030
,MTHONG BA'I CHOS LA RNAM GNYIS PO,

00:32:36.030 --> 00:32:39.520
Now MTHONG BA'I CHOS can mean

00:32:39.520 --> 00:32:42.240
something you saw at the path of seeing,

00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:44.573
but it can also mean dirsta-adirsta,

00:32:45.960 --> 00:32:49.800
seen in this life or
seen in the future life.

00:32:49.800 --> 00:32:51.260
And that's what it means here.

00:32:51.260 --> 00:32:54.453
So as far as, are you going to see it,

00:32:55.790 --> 00:32:57.030
as far as dirsta-adirsta

00:32:57.030 --> 00:33:02.030
when you do any kind
of...well, how should we say?

00:33:02.580 --> 00:33:05.480
anytime you commit a karma in this life,

00:33:05.480 --> 00:33:10.480
your won't go away is dirsta in this life.

00:33:10.670 --> 00:33:12.630
You pick it up in this life.

00:33:12.630 --> 00:33:15.110
Whatever karma you committed in this life,

00:33:15.110 --> 00:33:18.376
you pick up a don't go
away for that in this life.

00:33:18.376 --> 00:33:20.326
Dirsta, it's seen in this life.

00:33:21.262 --> 00:33:22.750
RNAM GNYIS PO

00:33:22.750 --> 00:33:25.411
And that could apply
to ZAG BCAS or ZAG MED

00:33:25.411 --> 00:33:26.620
in the Abhidharma system.

00:33:26.620 --> 00:33:30.920
Good karmas... impure
karmas or pure karmas

00:33:30.920 --> 00:33:33.758
which is a long subject.

00:33:33.758 --> 00:33:37.120
,KUN GYI [THAMS CAD] LAS DANG LAS KYI DE,

00:33:37.120 --> 00:33:41.060
Also, both types of chetana

00:33:41.060 --> 00:33:43.029
and chetayitva,

00:33:44.104 --> 00:33:46.050
chetana and chetayitva.

00:33:46.050 --> 00:33:48.413
We studied it a long time ago, yesterday.

00:33:49.571 --> 00:33:51.400
[student laughing]

00:33:51.400 --> 00:33:53.490
Chetana comes from √cit.

00:33:53.490 --> 00:33:54.952
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:33:54.952 --> 00:33:57.620
Chetana.

00:33:57.620 --> 00:33:58.920
Yeah. Yeah.

00:33:58.920 --> 00:34:01.460
Intention and intended.

00:34:01.460 --> 00:34:05.190
So that division, he says,

00:34:05.190 --> 00:34:09.070
whether you commit a karma mentally,

00:34:09.070 --> 00:34:12.140
or whether you commit
a karma because of what

00:34:12.140 --> 00:34:14.380
you were thinking, both of them,

00:34:14.380 --> 00:34:18.490
you still pick up a don't go away.

00:34:18.490 --> 00:34:21.720
Whether it's mental karma,
which is thinking karma,

00:34:21.720 --> 00:34:25.450
which is intention, or it's
the action of body or speech,

00:34:25.450 --> 00:34:27.640
which was intended by that,

00:34:28.540 --> 00:34:30.790
you still pick up a don't go away.

00:34:30.790 --> 00:34:34.091
This is all details of don't go aways.

00:34:35.544 --> 00:34:37.877
Avipranasha.

00:34:39.299 --> 00:34:41.200
,THA DAD PAR NI SKYE 'GYUR ZHING,

00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:42.480
This is cool.

00:34:42.480 --> 00:34:46.880
You get a separate don't go away
every time you make a karma.

00:34:46.880 --> 00:34:51.413
So you're basically collecting
don't go aways your whole life.

00:34:51.413 --> 00:34:55.260
Your whole life your pockets
filling up with don't go aways.

00:34:55.260 --> 00:34:58.650
Every tiny thing you do,
you get a new don't go away.

00:34:58.650 --> 00:35:00.060
It's discreet.

00:35:00.060 --> 00:35:03.250
It says here THA DAD, THA DAD PAR SKYE,

00:35:03.250 --> 00:35:04.923
it arises discreetly,

00:35:05.907 --> 00:35:08.145
,RNAM PAR SMIN KYANG GNAS PA YIN,

00:35:08.145 --> 00:35:10.040
This is really controversial.

00:35:10.040 --> 00:35:14.637
After the karma ripens, the
don't go away stays with you.

00:35:17.630 --> 00:35:19.469
Well, what's it do [laughs]?

00:35:19.469 --> 00:35:20.680
Don't ask me.

00:35:20.680 --> 00:35:25.260
He doesn't say, but
according to Abhidharma,

00:35:25.260 --> 00:35:27.560
the don't go away stays with you,

00:35:27.560 --> 00:35:30.773
even if the karma is
destroyed or it ripens,

00:35:31.640 --> 00:35:33.730
and it finishes.

00:35:33.730 --> 00:35:35.040
Even if the seed finishes,

00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:37.000
the don't go away stays with you somehow.

00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:40.330
So we must be collecting
zillions of don't go aways.

00:35:40.330 --> 00:35:44.300
What do they do if they don't hold
the karma anymore, I don't know.

00:35:44.300 --> 00:35:46.290
It's kind of like an empty pocket

00:35:46.290 --> 00:35:48.680
after you spend all your money.

00:35:48.680 --> 00:35:51.687
I guess you could still have the pocket.

00:35:51.687 --> 00:35:53.510
All right.

00:35:53.510 --> 00:35:56.810
Now the Abhidharma guy says, "Nagarjuna,

00:35:56.810 --> 00:35:58.233
you forgot to tell them how to get rid of

00:35:58.233 --> 00:36:00.230
your don't go aways."

00:36:00.230 --> 00:36:03.370
And Nagarjuna is like "ah,
yeah, let's talk about"

00:36:03.370 --> 00:36:06.470
So here's how to get rid
of your don't go aways,

00:36:06.470 --> 00:36:07.770
extra don't go aways.

00:36:07.770 --> 00:36:08.676
All right.

00:36:08.676 --> 00:36:09.701
,DE NI 'BRAS BU 'PHO BA DANG,

00:36:09.701 --> 00:36:11.581
,SHI BAR GYUR NA 'GAG PAR 'GYUR,

00:36:11.581 --> 00:36:13.020
The second part here is easy.

00:36:13.020 --> 00:36:14.300
If you're SHI BA,

00:36:14.300 --> 00:36:16.210
you lose your don't go aways.

00:36:16.210 --> 00:36:17.068
- [Student] If you die.

00:36:17.068 --> 00:36:20.148
- Yeah, if die, you lose
some don't go aways.

00:36:21.250 --> 00:36:22.880
Doesn't seem to make sense

00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:25.634
because you should be able to
carry it into your next life.

00:36:25.634 --> 00:36:28.081
'BRAS BU 'PHO BA means serious,

00:36:28.081 --> 00:36:33.081
heavy graduating karmic result.

00:36:34.157 --> 00:36:38.740
This refers to a stream enterer,

00:36:38.740 --> 00:36:41.440
once returner, non-returner, and arhat.

00:36:41.440 --> 00:36:44.290
These are called the four fruits.

00:36:44.290 --> 00:36:48.130
When the fruit is big, heavy good karma,

00:36:48.130 --> 00:36:52.880
heavy spiritual realizations, "yeah,
it could cancel your don't go aways."

00:36:52.880 --> 00:36:54.990
And I can, I don't know,

00:36:54.990 --> 00:36:59.805
but I'm imagining SBYOR LAM BZOD,

00:36:59.805 --> 00:37:01.920
the mastery level of SBYOR LAM.

00:37:01.920 --> 00:37:06.590
You can't go to a lower realm anymore,

00:37:06.590 --> 00:37:09.680
so they must've destroyed
your don't go aways.

00:37:09.680 --> 00:37:12.190
It must have damaged some
of your don't go aways.

00:37:12.190 --> 00:37:13.100
But then he just said

00:37:13.100 --> 00:37:17.111
that can only be lost when you
become an arhat, I don't know.

00:37:17.111 --> 00:37:18.019
Okay.

00:37:19.123 --> 00:37:21.223
,DE YI RNAM DBYE ZAG MED DANG,

00:37:21.223 --> 00:37:23.298
,ZAG DANG BCAS PAR SHES PAR BYA,

00:37:23.298 --> 00:37:26.520
You could have enlightened don't go aways

00:37:26.520 --> 00:37:30.813
and you can have sansaric don't go aways.

00:37:32.373 --> 00:37:34.010
Everyone in the room is going to sleep.

00:37:34.010 --> 00:37:36.860
Let's see if we can go on [Laughs].

00:37:37.780 --> 00:37:41.255
I like this picture, okay, Pachi?

00:37:43.090 --> 00:37:44.710
I built my Lama's house.

00:37:44.710 --> 00:37:48.018
It took me... Oh wait, there's
one more picture of him.

00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:52.900
Yeah. I built my Lama's house.

00:37:52.900 --> 00:37:56.330
I paid for it and I built it

00:37:56.330 --> 00:38:01.330
and no one came to help me.

00:38:01.490 --> 00:38:03.660
I mean, one guy helped me
for a day or something.

00:38:03.660 --> 00:38:05.460
So I was up on these high...,

00:38:05.460 --> 00:38:08.010
it's two stories high, I
was up in the third story

00:38:08.010 --> 00:38:10.600
on the ladder and I'll never forget it.

00:38:10.600 --> 00:38:12.740
It was winter, dead of winter.

00:38:12.740 --> 00:38:16.653
I'm up on the ladder,
painting the house like this.

00:38:17.562 --> 00:38:19.700
And these people would come,

00:38:19.700 --> 00:38:22.783
Mongolian old men and
they'd say "Hey, Mike."

00:38:22.783 --> 00:38:23.849
I'm like what?

00:38:23.849 --> 00:38:26.350
He said, "I got to go to the store."

00:38:26.350 --> 00:38:30.130
I'm like, "I'm painting the house
that no one's helping me paint."

00:38:30.130 --> 00:38:33.020
And he said, "But I'm going
to store, I need a ride.

00:38:33.020 --> 00:38:36.320
I was the SPYI PA'I RTA,

00:38:36.320 --> 00:38:40.640
I was the public horse of the
whole community, so anyway.

00:38:40.640 --> 00:38:42.400
So why am I talking about that?

00:38:42.400 --> 00:38:45.350
If you get high enough, you
leave the toolbox at the bottom.

00:38:45.350 --> 00:38:47.160
If you're working on the third story,

00:38:47.160 --> 00:38:49.260
you always forget some tool.

00:38:49.260 --> 00:38:51.780
And then you have to climb down
this very dangerous ladder,

00:38:51.780 --> 00:38:55.448
two stories, get the
screwdriver and go back up.

00:38:55.448 --> 00:38:58.340
And then you forgot the paint, you know.

00:38:58.340 --> 00:38:59.710
And you're by yourself.

00:38:59.710 --> 00:39:02.190
Anyway, what I'm saying
is if you get high enough,

00:39:02.190 --> 00:39:06.680
you can leave some of your
don't go aways behind.

00:39:06.680 --> 00:39:09.740
I don't know why that image, anyway.

00:39:09.740 --> 00:39:10.573
All right.

00:39:12.710 --> 00:39:14.993
Let's go to the next verse.

00:39:19.110 --> 00:39:24.110
So we start saying, we start thinking,

00:39:25.310 --> 00:39:27.610
well, then this whole don't go away thing

00:39:27.610 --> 00:39:31.360
is starting to sound a
little uncomfortable.

00:39:31.360 --> 00:39:34.640
This feels like really a lower idea

00:39:34.640 --> 00:39:38.700
that once you commit a
karma, it can't just go away.

00:39:38.700 --> 00:39:40.680
It starts to feel uncomfortable, right?

00:39:40.680 --> 00:39:42.474
This whole idea of a don't go away,

00:39:42.474 --> 00:39:45.570
you know, it sounds weird.

00:39:45.570 --> 00:39:48.780
Then suddenly Nagarjuna shifts gears.

00:39:48.780 --> 00:39:51.435
He says, following verse,

00:39:51.435 --> 00:39:53.294
,STONG PA NYID DANG TSAD MED DANG,

00:39:53.294 --> 00:39:56.593
,'KHOR BA DANG NI RTAG PA MIN,

00:39:56.593 --> 00:39:58.701
,LAS RNAMS CHUD MI ZA BA'I CHOS,

00:39:58.701 --> 00:40:00.876
,SANGS RGYAS KYIS NI BSTAN PA YIN,

00:40:00.876 --> 00:40:02.713
Who taught don't go aways?

00:40:02.713 --> 00:40:04.379
- [Student] The Buddha.
- The Buddha.

00:40:04.379 --> 00:40:07.490
So Nagarjuna says, "Hey,
don't think don't go aways

00:40:07.490 --> 00:40:10.790
are stupid idea, there's
a real don't go away."

00:40:10.790 --> 00:40:14.070
As he seems to shift gears
here, he's like look,

00:40:14.070 --> 00:40:17.287
I know you guys now, you don't have
much respect for don't go aways,

00:40:17.287 --> 00:40:19.630
but there is a real don't go away.

00:40:19.630 --> 00:40:21.810
Let me tell you about
the real don't go away.

00:40:21.810 --> 00:40:24.435
And then he starts to describe it.

00:40:25.417 --> 00:40:27.560
STONG PA NYID

00:40:27.560 --> 00:40:31.610
Don't think that just
because something is empty,

00:40:31.610 --> 00:40:34.573
it's going to destroy the don't go away.

00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:38.203
Don't go aways do exist.

00:40:39.300 --> 00:40:41.030
And they are empty.

00:40:41.030 --> 00:40:45.243
But that doesn't mean
they don't keep your seed.

00:40:46.080 --> 00:40:47.740
Okay?

00:40:47.740 --> 00:40:50.265
Don't think that don't go aways

00:40:51.630 --> 00:40:55.570
can't hold your karma
with you for lifetimes

00:40:56.550 --> 00:40:59.410
just because they are empty.

00:40:59.410 --> 00:41:02.210
That's a misunderstanding empty.

00:41:02.210 --> 00:41:05.380
When I say a don't go away is empty,

00:41:05.380 --> 00:41:09.530
I don't mean it doesn't work
because you guys keeps thinking

00:41:09.530 --> 00:41:11.340
that every time I say empty,

00:41:11.340 --> 00:41:14.670
you guys think it doesn't matter anymore.

00:41:14.670 --> 00:41:18.400
But when I say empty, I mean
it does matter [laughs].

00:41:18.400 --> 00:41:19.740
Don't go aways are empty.

00:41:19.740 --> 00:41:22.500
Therefore you better learn
about them and respect them

00:41:22.500 --> 00:41:24.160
because it means they work.

00:41:24.160 --> 00:41:25.920
It doesn't mean they don't work.

00:41:25.920 --> 00:41:29.181
So that's the first thing
Nagarjuna has to say.

00:41:29.181 --> 00:41:30.462
STONG PA NYID CHAD PA

00:41:30.462 --> 00:41:33.213
CHAD PA means...

00:41:35.340 --> 00:41:37.219
when we say BEM RIG RGYUN CHAD PA,

00:41:39.810 --> 00:41:42.653
when you cut off the flow
of something... anyway,

00:41:45.120 --> 00:41:47.155
let's say cut off.

00:41:48.189 --> 00:41:49.341
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:41:49.341 --> 00:41:50.720
- Terminate? Truncate.

00:41:50.720 --> 00:41:52.540
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:41:52.540 --> 00:41:55.960
It should be CHAD PA, STONG
PA NYID DANG CHAD PA DANG.

00:41:55.960 --> 00:41:57.340
Oh, that's... hm-hm.

00:41:57.340 --> 00:41:59.860
Yeah, that's certainly a mistake.

00:41:59.860 --> 00:42:03.294
By the way, I mixed the Tengyur
version and the Choney Lama's versions,

00:42:03.294 --> 00:42:07.070
so I could detect problems.

00:42:07.070 --> 00:42:09.160
I have the Choney Lama's version,

00:42:09.160 --> 00:42:11.140
you have the Tengyur version.

00:42:11.140 --> 00:42:14.790
And the reason I did that, so
I could detect any problems.

00:42:14.790 --> 00:42:16.247
So anyway,

00:42:16.247 --> 00:42:17.822
STONG PA NYID DANG CHAD PA DANG

00:42:17.822 --> 00:42:21.341
So don't think that's because it's empty

00:42:21.341 --> 00:42:24.877
your don't go away it's
just going to disappear.

00:42:24.877 --> 00:42:26.793
CHAD PA -- truncate.

00:42:26.793 --> 00:42:29.210
We had the two extremes,

00:42:29.210 --> 00:42:31.630
thinking things are unchanging

00:42:31.630 --> 00:42:34.885
and thinking things just stop.

00:42:34.885 --> 00:42:37.094
Third thing.

00:42:37.094 --> 00:42:38.855
'KHOR BA

00:42:40.338 --> 00:42:43.560
"You better figure out
this don't go away thing,"

00:42:43.560 --> 00:42:45.466
says Nagarjuna, "first of all,

00:42:45.466 --> 00:42:47.760
because the Buddha said it and secondly,

00:42:47.760 --> 00:42:51.900
because it is the king of
sansara. It runs sansara.

00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:55.453
Don't go aways run sansara.

00:42:55.453 --> 00:42:58.070
They are the bus drivers for sansara.

00:42:58.070 --> 00:43:01.290
The don't go aways in your karmic pocket

00:43:01.290 --> 00:43:03.980
are the bus driver of your sansara.

00:43:03.980 --> 00:43:06.430
So you goddamn better figur it out

00:43:06.430 --> 00:43:09.490
because they keep your karmas with you.

00:43:09.490 --> 00:43:13.050
So you better figure it out.
So he says this is not BS.

00:43:13.050 --> 00:43:15.530
This is real.
The Buddha talked about it.

00:43:15.530 --> 00:43:17.710
We have to figure it out

00:43:17.710 --> 00:43:20.100
because they are running your suffering.

00:43:20.100 --> 00:43:21.853
Last thing.

00:43:21.853 --> 00:43:23.210
RTAG PA MIN

00:43:23.210 --> 00:43:26.000
Don't think they are unchanging.

00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:28.260
That's not correct.

00:43:28.260 --> 00:43:33.260
Don't think that a karma stored over
time would have to be unchanging.

00:43:33.353 --> 00:43:34.970
That's also a misperception.

00:43:34.970 --> 00:43:39.160
The Buddha did say karma
can be stored over time

00:43:39.160 --> 00:43:40.570
and come back to you,

00:43:40.570 --> 00:43:43.570
that doesn't mean that
karma is unchanging.

00:43:43.570 --> 00:43:47.681
It just means it's replicating
or something like that.

00:43:47.681 --> 00:43:50.626
So what he's saying is
I've made a lot of fun

00:43:50.626 --> 00:43:55.070
of the Abhidharma guys in
a bunch of verses here,

00:43:55.070 --> 00:43:57.700
but actually they're pretty cool.

00:43:57.700 --> 00:44:01.803
This idea that you could,
that karma don't go away

00:44:02.960 --> 00:44:05.970
that's for real, that's for real.

00:44:05.970 --> 00:44:06.910
He says,

00:44:06.910 --> 00:44:10.997
"I just brought it up because
you guys think if it's empty,

00:44:10.997 --> 00:44:13.230
"a don't go away can't work.

00:44:13.230 --> 00:44:15.120
"But I want to tell you if it's empty,

00:44:15.120 --> 00:44:18.470
"that's the proof that it can
work and karma will stay with you,

00:44:18.470 --> 00:44:20.060
"so you better watch your karma.

00:44:20.060 --> 00:44:22.590
"This don't go away stuff is real."

00:44:22.590 --> 00:44:25.630
- Why? - Buddha said so.

00:44:25.630 --> 00:44:26.877
That's Nagarjuna.

00:44:30.810 --> 00:44:33.368
It seems like a long class,
but it's okay, right?

00:44:33.368 --> 00:44:35.361
All right, here we go.

00:44:35.361 --> 00:44:37.877
,GANG PHYIR LAS NI SKYE BA MED,

00:44:37.877 --> 00:44:39.802
,'DI LTAR RANG BZHIN MED DE'I PHYIR,

00:44:39.802 --> 00:44:41.451
,GANG PHYIR DE NI MA SKYES PA,

00:44:41.451 --> 00:44:45.043
,DE PHYIR CHUD ZAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:44:48.100 --> 00:44:52.259
Then Nagarjuna goes into why
a don't go away should work.

00:44:53.372 --> 00:44:55.680
Nagarjuna goes into why a
don't go away should work.

00:44:55.680 --> 00:44:58.317
And he says LAS NI SKYE BA MED,

00:44:59.600 --> 00:45:04.600
don't go aways work because
you cannot do karma.

00:45:06.780 --> 00:45:11.780
Don't go aways work because
you cannot do karma.

00:45:15.460 --> 00:45:20.460
Meaning which exists from its own side.

00:45:20.958 --> 00:45:24.791
So he's kicking, you know. Now he's
like, yay, finally, I confused you.

00:45:26.296 --> 00:45:27.129
[everyone laughing]

00:45:27.129 --> 00:45:28.170
I'll say it again.

00:45:28.170 --> 00:45:33.170
Don't go aways work because
karma... you cannot do karma.

00:45:33.690 --> 00:45:36.813
Don't go aways work because
you cannot do karma.

00:45:36.813 --> 00:45:38.240
'DI LTAR RANG BZHIN MED DE'I PHYIR

00:45:38.240 --> 00:45:39.640
- Why?

00:45:39.640 --> 00:45:42.960
- Because karma doesn't
have any nature of its own.

00:45:42.960 --> 00:45:44.962
It's coming from your seed.

00:45:44.962 --> 00:45:47.010
GANG PHYIR DE NI MA SKYES PA

00:45:47.010 --> 00:45:50.590
And because you cannot do karma,

00:45:50.590 --> 00:45:55.075
it's going to stay with
you without going away.

00:45:56.270 --> 00:45:58.670
Because you cannot do karma,

00:45:58.670 --> 00:46:02.660
it's going to stay with you
and cannot just go away.

00:46:02.660 --> 00:46:07.660
Because you cannot do karma,
you do get don't go aways.

00:46:08.280 --> 00:46:09.700
Got it?

00:46:09.700 --> 00:46:12.050
Because you cannot do karma,

00:46:12.050 --> 00:46:15.592
you do get those don't go aways.

00:46:15.592 --> 00:46:16.480
- [Christina] And that sounds like karma

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:19.100
don't go aways are the same thing.`

00:46:19.100 --> 00:46:23.200
- Uh. Don't go aways
keep karma on Christina,

00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:24.594
whoever Christina is.

00:46:24.594 --> 00:46:25.427
- [Christina] Like a glue?

00:46:25.427 --> 00:46:26.260
- Yeah, it's like a glue.

00:46:26.260 --> 00:46:28.269
This is a very Abhidharma idea.

00:46:28.269 --> 00:46:30.360
By the way, if you want to get,

00:46:30.360 --> 00:46:32.600
if you really want to ask questions,

00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:34.743
what keeps the glue on you?

00:46:34.743 --> 00:46:35.576
- [Christina] Right.

00:46:35.576 --> 00:46:38.470
- Then they, Abhidharma
says, THOB PA'I THOB PA.

00:46:38.470 --> 00:46:41.492
You got to have a glue for the glue.

00:46:41.492 --> 00:46:42.890
Then they say, then the other guy says,

00:46:42.890 --> 00:46:43.723
do you have THOB PA'I THOB PA'I THOB PA,

00:46:43.723 --> 00:46:45.270
do you have glue for
the glue for the glue?

00:46:45.270 --> 00:46:47.614
And they say, "Nope, it ends
at the glue for the glue."

00:46:47.614 --> 00:46:50.526
[everone laughing]

00:46:50.526 --> 00:46:51.594
Okay.

00:46:51.594 --> 00:46:52.475
So don't worry.

00:46:52.475 --> 00:46:54.381
You don't need glue for your glue.

00:46:54.381 --> 00:46:55.878
You don't need glues for your glue glue,

00:46:55.878 --> 00:46:58.808
but you do need glue for your glue.

00:46:58.808 --> 00:47:00.140
All right.

00:47:00.140 --> 00:47:03.620
I like this next picture.
It's called The Rules.

00:47:03.620 --> 00:47:05.190
Why stuff works?

00:47:06.320 --> 00:47:09.370
And the rules.

00:47:09.370 --> 00:47:14.370
I like to say the rules hold
true because they don't exist.

00:47:14.620 --> 00:47:17.110
You got to follow the rules of karma

00:47:17.110 --> 00:47:18.890
because they don't exist.

00:47:18.890 --> 00:47:22.990
Meaning even the laws of
karma are coming from you.

00:47:22.990 --> 00:47:25.915
Well, then Geshe-la they
should be adjustable.

00:47:27.560 --> 00:47:31.770
If the laws of karma are coming from me,

00:47:31.770 --> 00:47:33.470
then I should be able to do a good deed

00:47:33.470 --> 00:47:35.380
and get a bad result,

00:47:35.380 --> 00:47:37.440
you know, under weird circumstances.

00:47:37.440 --> 00:47:39.410
If it's coming from me,

00:47:39.410 --> 00:47:42.410
then I should be able to
mess with the laws of karma.

00:47:42.410 --> 00:47:44.250
And that's a fallacy.

00:47:44.250 --> 00:47:47.100
The fact that something's coming from you

00:47:47.100 --> 00:47:50.440
doesn't mean you can change it.

00:47:50.440 --> 00:47:52.750
That there's not patterns.

00:47:52.750 --> 00:47:56.080
That there's not inevitable patterns.

00:47:56.080 --> 00:48:00.630
The fact that something's
coming from you is not a proof

00:48:00.630 --> 00:48:03.980
that there are not
inevitable patterns in life.

00:48:03.980 --> 00:48:05.810
And that if you hurt someone,

00:48:05.810 --> 00:48:07.580
you're going to get hurt.

00:48:07.580 --> 00:48:09.730
- Are you creating that law? - Yes.

00:48:09.730 --> 00:48:12.720
- Can you change that law? - No.

00:48:12.720 --> 00:48:14.637
- Well, if it's coming
from you, I can change it.

00:48:14.637 --> 00:48:17.078
MA KHYAB - not necessarily.

00:48:18.480 --> 00:48:19.787
Okay?

00:48:19.787 --> 00:48:20.620
[hands clapping]

00:48:20.620 --> 00:48:22.990
We'll talk about it.

00:48:22.990 --> 00:48:24.260
It's a tough class.

00:48:24.260 --> 00:48:25.920
Listen to it a bunch of times.

00:48:25.920 --> 00:48:27.829
We're not done with our
examination of karma.

00:48:27.829 --> 00:48:29.878
We've got one more class to go.

00:48:29.878 --> 00:48:31.895
See you, next one.

